     1	"""Deterministic reference/Pangolin N-ablation atlas (GRCh38 / GENCODE v50).
     2	
     3	N masking measures cis-sequence sensitivity, NOT physical ASO occupancy or PSI.
     4	Each of four tissue splice-site probability channels is reported separately, averaged over its
     5	three released models, matching feng.titration.gpu_scores' channel selection.
     6	All public coordinates are 1-based inclusive. FaiFastaReader converts at I/O;
     7	mask slices convert in footprint_mask. Minus-strand input is reverse-complemented
     8	once; readout indices then follow transcript orientation.
     9	
    10	CLI: --smoke --output-dir DIR, or --config JSON --output-dir DIR.
    11	JSON: {"assembly":"GRCh38", "annotation":"GENCODE v50", "windows":[
    12	 {"locus":"id", "chrom":"chr5", "strand":"+", "center":70076574,
    13	  "distance":50, "sites":[{"position":70076574,"kind":"donor"}]}],
    14	 "grid":{"lengths":[18],"start":70076584,"end":70076601,"stride":1}}
    15	Sites and grid must be prespecified independently of measured outcomes. One
    16	absolute genomic tiling interval per config; use separate configs for distant
    17	loci. No inferred or outcome-selected splice sites are added by this engine.
    18	"""
